Please press a button on the selected transmitter in the next step.

device_ewneo_receiver_already_exists.description:
**This Easywave neo receiver has already been learned!**

The receiver is already used as **{device_name}** in Home Assistant.

🔄 **The device has been updated:**
• Old Easywave neo Index: {old_index}
• New Easywave neo Index: {new_index}

Please repeat the process and use a receiver that has not been learned yet.

device_receiver_confirm.description:
📥 **Easywave Receiver Configuration - Step 3/3**

**📋 Configuration:**
• Device: {device_name}
• Serial Number: {serial}
• RX11 Index: {rx11_index}
• Type: {receiver_kind}
• Mode: {operating_mode}

**🎛️ Buttons to create:**
{button_summary}

**📡 Learning Process:**

**1.** {learn_instructions}
**2.** Click 'Create & Send Code A'
**3.** System sends Code A to the receiver
**4.** Device is created in Home Assistant

💡 **Note:** After confirmation, the receiver will be automatically configured and button entities will be created.

ew_receiver_learn.description:
**STEP 1:** Put receiver into learning mode

{mode_instructions}

**Procedure:**
1. Press the learn button on the Easywave receiver
2. LED should flash (learning mode active)
3. Confirm with 'OK' when learning mode is active

**Configuration:**
- Device: {device_name}
- RX11 Index: {rx11_index}
- Type: {receiver_kind}
- Mode: {operating_mode}

ew_receiver_final_confirm.description:
**FINAL CONFIRMATION:**

The Easywave receiver is ready to be created:

**Device Data:**
- Name: {device_name}
- RX11 Index: {rx11_index}
- Type: {receiver_kind}
- Operating Mode: {operating_mode}
- Button Count: {button_count}

**Available Functions:**
{button_summary}

⚠️ **Important:** The communication test will be performed during creation.

